steps.instructions:
`masterVolume(0)` turns every sound off at once, `masterVolume(1)` turns them all back on, and `masterVolume()` with nothing in the brackets tells you the level it is at now. In `draw()`, next to the R line and outside `if (playing)` so it also works on the game-over screen:

```js
if (kb.presses('m')) {
  if (masterVolume() > 0) masterVolume(0);
  else masterVolume(1);
}
```

This step has no check; the game is finished without it.
